  ('af5e7085-aafb-4264-8351-ffc8d68f617a', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', '309ba1a2-eec4-402c-9562-5fe99e4431be', '06451e70-3f92-45d7-b3ca-febb0d493d17', 'cf2d9caa-5ae4-46df-9954-b637993032da', '95b8bc81-1f6b-4a5c-845b-a3afb375fa3a', $qbx$What commitment do Jamie’s words offer to the people with special needs? As time passed, Jamie’s influence on his town became undeniable. His achievements in sports and arts, combined with his promotion activity brought about significant changes in the attitudes of the town towards people with special needs. COMPETENCY-BASED LEARNING “You've changed this town, Jamie,” Mayor Thompson said, shaking his hand firmly. “We're proud to call you one of our own.” With tears of joy in his eyes, Jamie looked out at the faces gathered before him, each one proof of the power of resilience and hope. Resilience is the art of bouncing back stronger, no matter how hard the challenges are. aes Use Cordova Smart Class Software on the smart board in class to explore the theme of sensitivity towards all. TIMEFOR DISCUSSION | The only true disability is the inability to accept and respect differences. SP EXERGIS [Use Cordova Smart Class Software on the smart board in class to do these exercises. ] (According to NEP Guidelines) [fy ANSWER ORALLY (Sensitivity Towards All) Read these words aloud: dribbling, inclusivity, scepticism, undeniable, campaigns People with special needs sometimes feel left out when they encounter physical barriers in public places. Do you agree? Why/Why not? [fy MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS A. Tick (V) the correct options. (Understanding, Analysing) 1. What initially attracted Jamie to the community centre? a) He learnt about art classes. ion ) He wanted to join a music band. Cc ( ( ( (d ) ) He discovered a wheelchair basketball team. He was looking for a quiet place to study. UOU00 2. Read the given statements. Choose the correct option. Assertion (A): Jamie’s participation in arts helped change the community’s view of people with special needs. Reason (R): Jamie showcased the talents of individuals with special needs, fostering a more inclusive community. English-8$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-14-076Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 8, NULL);
